{
  "model": "MK50",
  "line": "jordan",
  "displayName": "Jordan Mark 50 Series back pressure regulator",
  "match": ["mk50", "mark 50", "mk50hp", "mk51", "mark 51", "jordan 50"],
  "source": { "doc": "mk50_51.pdf", "page": "3 and 4", "section": "Ordering Schematic with the spring ranges and Cv tables" },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, model dash size dash body then a slash and ten code characters, the separators exactly as the sheet's header row prints them. Four models on one sheet: 50 standard, 50HP high pressure, 50QC quick change and 51 large diaphragm. The spring tables are printed for 50 and 50QC together, for 50HP and for 51, banded by size; the 50QC column is not separately distinguished, so it rides the 50 table, held for John. The Cv ladder is constrained per size from the Cv values and maximum differential pressures table, downward only: the low flow note says a smaller valve's Cv can be supplied in a larger valve, so only above-size Cvs refuse. The sheet's asterisk on the 51's 1/2-5 spring, must use elastomer diaphragm, is enforced against the 316 diaphragm; Jorlon's class is not stated on this sheet, so Jorlon stays allowed and is flagged for John. There is no 1-1/4 inch row on this sheet, unlike the Mark 60 one. The prose options, handwheel, grain processing and cryogenic housing, have no schematic position and so no place in the code.",
